Good day, folks!

Thanks for the moral support; Indeed, I tried to have a more realistic
outlook on explore mode, but eventually, I would like to ascend a
character without any help more than a few spoilers.  But Voke, the
level 11 Valkyrie wasn't the one to do it.  This time around, I took
my "Die y/n" prompt like a man and ended her life when she was mauled
to death by a Large mimic while naked and unarmed on level 4 of
Sokoban.  Not to turn this into a YASD post, but that mimic wouldn't
let her retreat, so she valiantly fought to the pitiful end.

I do feel a bit better about explore mode, but I doubt I'll use it
regularly-- Sometimes it's better to just die.  Maybe next time I'm in
a similarly bleak situation I'll resort to explore before the end and
do as Ray suggests and try out a crazy strategy, so next time
something similar happens I can find a way out.. Though, much like the
Sokoban levels themselves, some situations are intractable long before
you realize what you've done wrong.

As a bit of a follow up to Derek's point, it's not that my game was /
actually/ tainted.. It was tainted in my mind, and spiritually, by the
accidental use of explore mode.  Though, again, reading the posts here
I've come to a more reasonable and realistic assessment of explore
mode and its valid experimental uses.  But after a good 15 years on
and off of playing nethack, one of these days I'd like to ascend a
character, one that will go in the high score table which I may or may
not print out and hang on my wall like a graduate degree certificate
or some other great honor.

Thanks for all of your help, folks, and I'll see you soon, hopefully
with a YAAP!

-Eric


